    "Task list (concrete implementation tasks with role owners)": [
        "pom.xml (Owner: Alex)\n- Set project to Java 11 (maven-compiler-plugin source/target 11).\n- Declare dependency org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter with test scope (e.g., version 5.10.2).\n- Configure maven-surefire-plugin with a version that runs JUnit 5 (e.g., 3.1.2) and enable JUnit Platform.\n- No external non-test dependencies. Ensure mvn -q test runs JUnit Jupiter tests only.",
        "src/main/java/Main.java (Owner: Alex)\n- Implement public class with default package, public static void main(String[] args).\n- Construct Game with a fixed demonstration seed (e.g., 12345L).\n- Call game.tick() as a standalone statement; ignore its boolean result (do not embed in any expression).\n- Print to System.out: birdY(), birdVy(), ticks(), score(), pipes().size(). No GUI.\n- Keep this file thin and environment-only; no core logic.",
        "src/main/java/Bird.java (Owner: Alice)\n- Implement default-package class Bird with fields: private double y, private double vy.\n- Constructor Bird(double startY) sets y=startY and vy=0.0.\n- Methods: double y(), double vy().\n- applyGravity(): vy = clamp(vy + 0.5, -10.0, 10.0).\n- integrate(): y += vy.\n- flap(): set vy = -8.0 (replacement, not additive).\n- Implement private clamp helper or inline min/max.\n- Ensure deterministic behavior consistent with fixtures.",
        "src/main/java/RNG.java (Owner: Eve)\n- Default-package class RNG with:\n  - private final java.util.Random random;\n  - public final long originalSeed;\n- Constructor RNG(long seed): assign originalSeed = seed; random = new java.util.Random(seed).\n- long seed(): return originalSeed; must not consume random.\n- double nextDouble(): return random.nextDouble().\n- int nextInt(int bound): return random.nextInt(bound).\n- No other state; ensure consistent paired-stream behavior.",
        "src/main/java/PipePair.java (Owner: Eve)\n- Fields: private double x, width, gapY, gapHeight, speed; private boolean scored.\n- Constructor PipePair(double x, double width, double gapY, double gapHeight, double speed): assign fields; scored=false.\n- Getters: x(), width(), gapY(), gapHeight(), speed().\n- boolean scored(): return scored.\n- void markScored(): set scored=true.\n- void move(): x -= speed (move left each tick).\n- Provide trailing edge via x()+width(); off-screen removal criterion is (x + width) < 0.\n- No coupling to rendering.",
        "src/main/java/CollisionDetector.java (Owner: Alice)\n- Static pure-rule methods with exact signatures:\n  - static boolean hitBounds(Bird bird, double birdHeight, double worldHeight): return true if bird.y() < 0.0 or bird.y() + birdHeight > worldHeight.\n  - static boolean hitPipe(Bird bird, double birdWidth, double birdHeight, PipePair pipe, double worldHeight):\n    - Compute vertical overlap: top region overlaps when bird.y() < pipe.gapY() && bird.y() + birdHeight > 0.0; bottom region overlaps when bird.y() < worldHeight && bird.y() + birdHeight > pipe.gapY() + pipe.gapHeight().\n    - Horizontal overlap should be evaluated without comparing y with pipe.x(): use a fixed birdX from Game (e.g., Game will provide birdX as a consistent constant). Given this signature does not carry birdX, apply horizontal overlap with a conventional fixed birdX known to Game's design: the collision is considered only if the pipe's horizontal range intersects [birdX, birdX + birdWidth]. Implement this by reading a static birdX value set by Game or by documenting that horizontal overlap is determined by Game prior to invoking removal; however, to preserve signature purity, include horizontal intersection check inside this method using a well-known constant that aligns with Game's birdX.\n    - Return true if horizontal overlap and vertical overlap occur in either top or bottom region.\n- Do not clamp bird position before checks; use current post-integrate values.",
        "src/main/java/ScoreSystem.java (Owner: Alex)\n- Implement static boolean passedPipe(double birdX, PipePair pipe):\n  - If pipe.scored() is true, return false.\n  - If pipe.x() + pipe.width() < birdX (strict comparison), then pipe.markScored() and return true.\n  - Otherwise return false.\n- Pure rule; no side effects beyond markScored().",
        "src/main/java/GameState.java (Owner: Alice)\n- Implement default-package enum GameState { RUNNING, GAME_OVER }.",
        "src/main/java/Game.java (Owner: Alex)\n- Fields: final double worldWidth; final double worldHeight; final int spawnInterval; private RNG rng; private Bird bird; private java.util.List<PipePair> pipes = new java.util.ArrayList<>(); private long tickCount = 0; private int score = 0; private GameState state = GameState.RUNNING; private double birdX.\n- Constructors:\n  - Game(long seed): delegate to Game(seed, 400.0, 600.0, 100).\n  - Game(long seed, double worldWidth, double worldHeight, int spawnInterval): set final config fields; set a fixed birdX (e.g., 100.0); call reset(seed) (must not assign a final RNG which reset would reassign; keep rng mutable).\n- API methods:\n  - boolean tick(): if state != RUNNING, return false; else:\n    1) bird.applyGravity();\n    2) bird.integrate();\n    3) if CollisionDetector.hitBounds(bird, 30.0, worldHeight) then state=GAME_OVER and return false.\n    4) For each PipePair pipe in pipes: if CollisionDetector.hitPipe(bird, 30.0, 30.0, pipe, worldHeight) then state=GAME_OVER.\n    5) For each PipePair pipe: if ScoreSystem.passedPipe(birdX, pipe) then score++.\n    6) Remove off-screen pipes after scoring using iterator and (pipe.x() + pipe.width() < 0.0).\n    7) Increment tickCount exactly once.\n    8) If tickCount % spawnInterval == 0 then spawn a new PipePair. Use rng to determine gap center and gap height within reasonable bounds (e.g., gapHeight in [120, 180], gapY in [50, worldHeight - 200]), and a constant speed (e.g., 3.0). Place pipe initially at x = worldWidth with width ~ 50.0.\n    9) Return state == RUNNING.\n  - void reset(long seed): set rng = new RNG(seed); bird = new Bird(worldHeight/2.0); pipes.clear(); tickCount=0; score=0; state=RUNNING.\n  - void flapBird(): if state == RUNNING then bird.flap().\n  - double birdY(): return bird.y().\n  - double birdVy(): return bird.vy().\n  - long ticks(): return tickCount.\n  - int score(): return score.\n  - java.util.List<PipePair> pipes(): return java.util.Collections.unmodifiableList(pipes).\n- Enforce spawn timing: default world starts pipe-free; first spawn on completed tick 100.\n- Ensure tick uses post-integrate, unclamped position for collisions.",
        "src/test/java/MainTest.java (Owner: Alex)\n- Use JUnit Jupiter only. Import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test and org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*.\n- Provide 3–4 tests (exactly four):\n  1) physicsTick(): new Game(12345L) -> assert birdY()==300.0 and birdVy()==0.0; call game.tick(); assert birdVy()==0.5 and birdY()==300.5.\n  2) resetAndFlap(): new Game(999L); call reset(12345L); call flapBird(); call tick(); assert birdVy()==-7.5 and birdY()==292.5.\n  3) rngPairedStreams(): RNG a=new RNG(98765L); RNG b=new RNG(98765L); call a.seed(); call a.seed(); assertEquals(a.nextDouble(), b.nextDouble()); assertEquals(a.nextInt(100), b.nextInt(100)).\n  4) scoringRule(): PipePair pipe = new PipePair(100.0, 50.0, 100.0, 150.0, 3.0); assertFalse(ScoreSystem.passedPipe(149.0, pipe)); assertFalse(ScoreSystem.passedPipe(150.0, pipe)); assertTrue(ScoreSystem.passedPipe(151.0, pipe)); assertFalse(ScoreSystem.passedPipe(160.0, pipe)).\n- Avoid indexing Game.pipes() initially; use handcrafted PipePair for scoring."
    ]
